            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0607" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.001C13/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Texas</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moody</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Austin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-06">December 6, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:50
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your wire December 5th. At the time your telegram of July 20th was received John
                    A. Valls was District Judge of Webb County. Since that time he has resigned as
                    District Judge and I have appointed him to his old position of District
                    Attorney. At the time your former wire was received I took this matter up with
                    Judge Valls through the then District Attorney R. L. Bobbitt who is now Attorney
                    General of Texas. I was advised that Mr. Valls had said that he would make no
                    effort to arrest or otherwise embarrass General Calles on his trip through
                    Texas. There were no charges pending against Calles then <pb facs="0608" n="514"
                        xml:id="pg514"/> and I feel certain there are none pending now. I believe
                    the State Department can place confidence in the statements made by Judge Valls
                    last July.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dan Moody</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
